{"type":"Feature","properties":{"kind":"port_limits","cargo":[],"osm":["relation/10507292","way/1317078648","way/1369970977","way/257587851"],"source":"Derived: the convex hull of this port's terminals from OpenStreetMap, grown by 300 m, then cut to the water OpenStreetMap maps inside it (the sea within its coastline, rivers, docks and basins), with the terminals kept whole","licence":"ODbL-1.0","reviewed_at":"2026-11-23","clip":"water","note":"OpenStreetMap maps no port limits for Hong Kong. These are the hull of the terminals below, from Kwai Tsing to the River Trade Terminal, grown by 300 m and cut to the sea OpenStreetMap maps inside it, with the terminals kept whole: the Kwai Tsing basin, the Rambler Channel, the channels round Tsing Yi and Ma Wan, and Urmston Road off Tuen Mun. Tsing Yi, Ma Wan and the Tsuen Wan and Tuen Mun shores are land and left out. A scan of OpenStreetMap finds no homes, schools, hospitals or places of worship inside. Eleven residential areas on the New Territories shore west of Tsuen Wan, Pearl Island Garden and Hong Kong Gold Coast among them, reach in where they are drawn over the water, by about 1,230 m² in all, with 12 m² of an apartment block. The named places are Pillar Point, under the River Trade Terminal, the Tai Kok Tau headland on Tsing Yi's shore, lot outlines and a label on the terminals, some 40 rocks and islets in the channels, and slivers of Ma Wan's and Lantau's shores."},"geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[114.122796,22.321242],[114.122549,22.321368],[114.122406,22.321133],[114.121631,22.321528],[114.12172,22.321785],[114.121524,22.322388],[114.122468,22.323431],[114.122656,22.323219],[114.122848,22.32341],[114.124989,22.321472],[114.125244,22.321318],[114.12564,22.321161],[114.126132,22.321003],[114.126447,22.320939],[114.126913,22.320891],[114.127229,22.320887],[114.127644,22.320904],[114.128046,22.320957],[114.128481,22.321045],[114.12897,22.321214],[114.129169,22.321333],[114.129329,22.321441],[114.129558